      "side": 1,
      "message": "`depths()` accepts any `u64` that fits a `usize`, and so do the template ellipsis counts read further down. A depth drives `value_match`\u0027s recursion (phase.rs), and an ellipsis count feeds `drivers`\u0027 arithmetic (pattern.rs).\n\nReproduced: `tmpl`\u0027s compiled template depth set to `u64::MAX`, then a call with a list nested a million deep, made through `%syntax-build`, a primitive a `syntax-case` transformer links legitimately. That aborted with \"has overflowed its stack\" (`value_match` at depth 18446744073709541687). With the original depth of 1 it\u0027s refused cleanly. The existing \"template depth \u003d MAX is refused\" test only passes because of a different error (\"match is corrupt\").\n\nBound depths and ellipsis counts at decode by `MAX_DECODED_NESTING`. Real ones are small.",
      "revId": "060ee05cbaf46b808397560b4cf19185d2be80b2",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
