      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T14:03:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`Pattern::remap`, and `Template::remap` below it, recurse once per level with no `stacker::maybe_grow`, though `build` and the walk at the top of the file use it. So the decoder\u0027s 2,000-level limit doesn\u0027t stop the remap from overflowing a small stack.\n\nReproduced: a `twice` clause pattern 1,999 lists deep aborted on a 2 MB test thread (opt-level 1), with thousands of `Pattern::remap` frames in gdb. 500, 999 and 1,500 were fine. Source patterns are capped at 1,000, so this is new with the doubled limit. The existing deep tests use 200,000, which decode refuses, so nothing exercises the limit itself. Wrap both in `maybe_grow` (or lower the limit), and add a test at the limit.",
      "revId": "060ee05cbaf46b808397560b4cf19185d2be80b2",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
